    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d58">

                <pb facs="0189" n="93" xml:id="pg93"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51 W 89France/297: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Herrick</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-05-06T18:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 6, 1926—6
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received May 6—2:55 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>178. After sending my 173, May 5th, I met Briand,<anchor n="3" xml:id="d58-f1"/>
                    who, without any remark on my part, raised this very point that prior
                    ratification by us would facilitate his task and said that in view of the
                    ratification of the other agreements he hoped our Senate would act quickly on
                    the French one.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Herrick</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d58-f1" n="3" xml:id="d58-f1-content">
                <p>Aristide Briand, French President of the Council and Minister for Foreign
                    Affairs.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
